  "cover_link": "https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/marveldatabase/images/7/7b/Strange_Tales_Vol_1_120.jpg",
  "plot_summary": "Johnny is reading a newspaper article about the X-Men and wonders what it would be like to meet them, in particular, the Iceman, but Reed points out that it won't be as easy as it sounds, as despite them being mutants (who are born with their power), nothing much is known about them, especially their true identities.&nbsp; But for the moment, Johnny decides he isn't going to worry about it, as he's promised his girlfriend, Doris, a boat ride around Manhattan island, little knowing that Bobby Drake/Iceman is planning to take the same cruise.\n\nHowever, Bobby finds himself too late to catch the boat and has to use his ice powers to get on board before it retreats too far from the harbor.&nbsp; There, he finds plenty of women, and though <i>most</i> of them seem to already have dates, he spots one alone by the ship's railing.&nbsp; It happens to be Doris Evans, and when Johnny returns after a moment, he shows off his flame powers to impress (and scare off) the newcomer, who immediately recognizes him as the Human Torch.\n\nBobby isn't happy about the snub, secretly knowing he could have impressed Doris with his <i>own</i> powers, but none of it soon matters, as, seconds later, Bobby bumps into a couple of guys who he doesn't realize are actually crooks, sent aboard the ship to sabotage its ability to contact the shore for help.\n\nOnce done, a smaller boat approaches, filled with armed men, and soon, a pirate named Captain Barracuda (complete with eye patch) climbs aboard.&nbsp; At gunpoint, he demands the passengers turn over their wallets and jewels, prompting both Human Torch and Iceman to spring into action (Johnny first ushering Doris into an inner cabin for her safety).&nbsp; In seconds, both heroes race toward the upper deck where Captain Barracuda and his men are.\n\nBy the time the Human Torch and Iceman both arrive on deck together, the Captain has already been tipped off to their presence.&nbsp; Barracuda is clever and orders his men to try and use their powers against them, and indeed, unused to working together, the flame and ice powers begin to interfere with each other.\n\nBarracuda directs his men to train a fire hose on Iceman, which serves to encase the young hero in a block of ice.&nbsp; The Human Torch quickly steps in to try and melt the icy outer layer, but Barracuda orders his men to fire at the flying teen, claiming that his flame will soon burn itself out.\n\nBarracuda orders his men to throw a canvas over the Human Torch, and even though it is not made of asbestos, which allows Johnny to burn through it quickly, the effort results in a fire on board the ship.&nbsp; He's forced to stop his attack on the pirate and focus on preventing the fire from spreading, which he knows both begins and ends with the canvas.&nbsp; He tries to throw the flaming material overboard, but Barracuda's men push him over as well.&nbsp; He plunges into the water, now completely depowered, and furthermore, unless Iceman can pull himself free, he knows the fire will soon spread and endanger the lives of everyone on board.\n\nWhile both the pirates and passengers wonder what they'll do, Iceman finally is able to spring into action, knowing that dealing with the onboard fire is his first order of business.&nbsp; He fashions snowballs which he rolls over the flaming deck and then hurls them at the bewildered pirates.&nbsp; Iceman seems about to get the upper hand against the pirates, but Barracuda once again outsmarts him by pouring gasoline over the ice, knowing that it will melt it quickly.&nbsp; Iceman's feet also begin to melt, allowing Barracuda's men to move toward him.\n\nBut at that moment, the Human Torch returns, having dried himself quickly by entering the ship's hot chimney -- he's back in action, and between him and the now-encouraged passengers, it seems as if the pirate henchmen will soon be rounded up.\n\nBut Barracuda isn't going easily, and he's somehow found Doris to use as a hostage.&nbsp; He retreats with her back to his smaller boat and seems about to get away (as Johnny is afraid to act for fear of hurting Doris).&nbsp; But even as Barracuda laughs in triumph, he finds his boat blocked by icebergs in the water.&nbsp; His boat is stuck, and in seconds a huge chunk of ice grows up out of the water and lifts the boat into the air.&nbsp; It isn't going <i>anywhere</i>!\n\nHis surprise gives Johnny the chance to swoop down and grab Doris, leaving Captain Barracuda alone on his boat atop the mound of ice.&nbsp; As the pirate rages, Johnny assures him he won't be alone for long -- he's about to summon a police launch to come and keep him company.\n\nIn the ensuing chaos, Iceman decides he's seen enough and fashions a sort of floating ice pathway that allows him to return to shore.&nbsp; And indeed, after ensuring Doris is safe, Johnny searches the ship for Iceman but finds no trace of him.&nbsp; He laments that he still doesn't know who Iceman really is.\n\nDoris and he wonder if they might even have bumped into him, never suspecting who he actually was...",
  "grade_one_liner": "FIXME - write something - is this showing up?",
  "subtitle": "FIXME - write something",
  "review_text": "A largely by-the-book first meeting between two of Marvel's teenage heroes, apparently requested by many readers, so this was in response.&nbsp; The introduction of Captain Barracuda was a nice addition, and I know we'll be seeing him again a few times.&nbsp; He didn't panic when he realized he was up against two super-powered defenders of the ship and used his brain to outwit them, despite it ultimately being in a losing effort.\n\nThere was nothing really bad in this offering, but it hardly will rise to the top of anyone's top-100 list either.&nbsp; It was nice to see them together.&nbsp; I don't know how many times they team up in the years ahead.&nbsp; I'm pretty sure the X-Men guest star in the FF coming up soon, and the pair also share a <i>Marvel Team-Up</i> issue against Equinox years later, but as for other appearances together, I guess we'll see...\n\n\n[BOTTOM_LINE]\n<b>FIXME</b>",
  "highlight": "FIXME - write something"
}